    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (85.34) is the clear focal point of the LawDog attack. Facing Whisenhunt in a favorable matchup, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a strong SP_xERA of 5.60 and a premium spot in the two-hole, cementing his status as our elite anchor. We are also projecting significant production from **Daulton Varsho** (70.98), whose matchup against the vulnerable Klassen (6.12 xERA) provides a massive 19% SP skill boost, making him our top-performing outfielder. **Bryce Harper** (65.42) remains a high-floor start despite a L/L matchup, as his elite xwOBA (0.389) and clean-up duties against Gibson, C provide enough stability to override the handedness disadvantage.\n\nThe benching of **Gleyber Torres** (38.19) was the most difficult decision of the morning. While he holds a prime leadoff spot, his 38.19 score failed to reach our 40-point efficiency floor due to an unfavorable matchup against Ashcraft, B and a significant 18% SP skill penalty. We are prioritizing the higher output potential of **Jonathan Aranda** (59.37) and **Masyn Winn** (58.63), both of whom clear the threshold comfortably thanks to better SP matchups. As a reminder, **Will Smith** and **Matt Chapman** remain completely off the board due to active IL designations; ensure no late-breaking alerts shift their status, though they are currently non-factors.\n\nRisk management is central to today\u2019s lineup, particularly regarding the late-order bats. **Yainer Diaz** (54.77) and **Justin Crawford** (48.54) both occupy the #9 hole, which inherently caps their scoring ceiling. While we are starting **Justin Crawford** to chase his elite speed potential\u2014a critical scarcity in our 5x5 Roto chase\u2014he remains a marginal play. Watch the wind patterns and final lineup confirmations for **Lawrence Butler** (45.73); his platoon disadvantage against Lynch IV makes him a volatile piece of the puzzle, and any further negative movement in his profile could necessitate a swap to prioritize high-floor efficiency over raw volume.",
